u trouble  and the  stretch across different planets with  totally different rules of gravity and  if that's not chaotic enough for you you  can crank things up in the games track  editor you can start your engines on the  13th  now let's slow things down a bit with  stardew valley calling it an indie  Harvest Moon is a disservice because  this farming simulator also tacks on  fishing cooking crafting and romance  options you can even explore  procedurally generated mines to find all  sorts of gems and minerals stardew  valley was already a hit on pc earlier  this year and now it's making its way to  consoles you can take up your farming  tools on ps4 on the 13th and on Xbox one  on the 14th and those are the games  we'll be playing this week as always  remember that release dates are based on  retailer listings and are subject to  change but that's gonna do it for this  episode of new releases and for the year  thanks for tuning in guys and I'll be  back with more in 2017  [Music]

